Good. The package copy is done.

Now create the new deterministic validator:

consumption_inventory_graph/05_validators/validate_schema_freeze.py

This script is separate from check_consistency.py.

Purpose:
- check_consistency.py checks low-level structural consistency.
- validate_schema_freeze.py checks the agreed Consumption Inventory Graph schema/model freeze criteria.

Important:
- Read from consumption_inventory_graph only.
- Do not read from model_linkml.
- Do not modify any schema/policy/generated files.
- Do not change schema logic.
- Do not change edge logic.
- Only create validate_schema_freeze.py.

Inputs:
- consumption_inventory_graph/03_schema/account_graph.yaml
- consumption_inventory_graph/03_schema/edge_policy.yaml
- consumption_inventory_graph/03_schema/classification_rules.yaml
- consumption_inventory_graph/03_schema/business_validation_rules.yaml
- consumption_inventory_graph/04_generated/account_graph.schema.json
- consumption_inventory_graph/04_generated/visual_schema_v2.json
- consumption_inventory_graph/04_generated/visjs_model_graph.json

Validate these areas:

A. Account taxonomy
PASS only if:
- canonical account class enum has Human, NonHuman, Unknown
- canonical account subtype enum has Human, ServiceAccount, Batch, Unknown
- classification rules support Human/Human, NonHuman/ServiceAccount, NonHuman/Batch, Unknown/Unknown
- Unknown/Unknown is review-required

B. Related controlled classifications
PASS only if:
- HumanAccount, ServiceAccount, BatchAccount are not physical schema classes in account_graph.yaml
- canonical edge labels exist in edge_policy.yaml:
  ACCESSED
  IN_DATABASE
  CATALOGUED_AS
  HAS_IDENTITY
  BELONGS_TO
  ACCOUNTABLE_TO
  HAS_OWNER
  OWNED_BY
  ASSIGNED_CI
  HAS_XCOM_TARGET
  RESOLVES_TO_APP
  IS_SANDPIT

C. Core graph structure
PASS only if edge_policy.yaml supports:
- Account -> ACCESSED -> Table
- Table -> IN_DATABASE -> Database
- Table -> CATALOGUED_AS -> CommDataIQAsset
- Account -> HAS_IDENTITY -> Identity
- Account -> ACCOUNTABLE_TO -> DirectoryPerson
- ConfigurationItem -> HAS_OWNER or OWNED_BY -> DirectoryPerson
- DirectoryPerson -> BELONGS_TO -> BusinessUnit
- ConfigurationItem -> RESOLVES_TO_APP -> ApplicationService
- Account -> HAS_XCOM_TARGET -> XCOMSystem
- Database -> IS_SANDPIT -> SandpitRecord

D. Conditional logic
PASS only if:
- IS_SANDPIT is Teradata-only
- IS_SANDPIT is not materialised when sandpit fields are null
- HAS_XCOM_TARGET is Batch-only or explicitly unsupported for Human, ServiceAccount, Unknown
- HAS_XCOM_TARGET is not materialised when xcom_remote is null
- CI/Owner/App paths are not supported for Human and Unknown
- Unknown/Unknown is review-required
- Unknown/Unknown only allows data access when source values are reliable

E. Identity -> DirectoryPerson decision
PASS only if:
- no active canonical edge exists from Identity to DirectoryPerson
- no active visual edge exists from Identity/AADIdentity to DirectoryPerson
- if disabled/unsupported notes exist, they explain this is avoided because it conflates account identity with ownership/contact person

F. Validation artefact alignment
PASS only if:
- generated JSON schema exists and is readable
- visual schema / visjs model exists and is readable
- visual/model graph has 13 nodes and 20 edges
- no orphan visual edges exist

Output:
Print a clean table:

Area | Result | Details

At the end print either:

SCHEMA FREEZE VALIDATION: PASS

or:

SCHEMA FREEZE VALIDATION: FAIL

Also write JSON output to:

consumption_inventory_graph/06_reports/schema_freeze_validation_result.json

Rules:
- deterministic Python only
- no LLM calls
- use yaml.safe_load and json only
- parser must tolerate existing key names in edge_policy.yaml such as source_vertex/target_vertex or source/target
- if any check fails, exit code 1
- if all checks pass, exit code 0

After creating it, run:

cd consumption_inventory_graph
python3 05_validators/validate_schema_freeze.py

Return:
1. whether the script was created
2. full terminal output
3. whether the JSON result file was created
4. any failures
